      "headline": {
        "en": "US insurance regulators defend oversight of insurers' growing private credit ties",
        "zh": "美国保险监管机构为对保险公司日益增长的私人信贷关联的监管辩护"
      },
      "summary": {
        "en": "The National Association of Insurance Commissioners responded to Senator Elizabeth Warren's concerns about insurers' ties to private investment firms and private credit exposure. The NAIC said it has strengthened asset-adequacy testing, reinsurance oversight, introduced a 45 per cent risk-based capital charge for residual interests in structured securities, and created a process to assess credit rating providers' methodologies. Insurers' private credit exposure rose from $386bn in 2014 to $849bn in 2024, according to the article.",
        "zh": "美国全国保险监督官协会（NAIC）回应了参议员Elizabeth Warren对保险公司与私人投资公司关联及私人信贷敞口的担忧。NAIC表示已加强资产充足性测试、再保险监管，对结构性证券剩余权益引入45%的风险基础资本计提，并建立了评估信用评级机构方法和映射是否适当的正式流程。文章称，保险公司的私人信贷敞口从2014年的3860亿美元增至2024年的8490亿美元。"
      },
